Subject: [PATCH] Cantilever Case 7: planar trusses on the faces, member-driven
 CadQuery and SolidWorks models

to/truss2d.py fits the face trusses (mirror pair) and the face layers (the base
on y = 0: plate, bar, fork with arms inclined to the xy plane), each as a planar
truss in its own plane; to/swtruss.py builds the models: mitred flat bars, one
corner radius, depths by volume; the CadQuery script is driven by the parameters,
the SolidWorks sketches (Truss on the Front Plane, Base on the Top Plane) by
joints, widths, R, t and tb (global variables). Stand-in: line-to-line distance
dimensions, sgCOLINEAR, sgPERPENDICULAR. Case7/results: detail-4 scripts,
STEP/STL, stand-in log, fitted structures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
